+I replaced the synchronous `requests.get(...)` calls with `treq.get(...)`, and updated the Prometheus helper functions to work with `treq`’s Twisted-style asynchronous responses by reading the body via `treq.content(...)` and decoding JSON from that body. I also added the `treq` import and the Twisted `inlineCallbacks`/`returnValue` helpers needed to keep the existing function names and call sites intact while making the HTTP calls compatible with `treq`.

